# IT Asset Management and Usage Policy
**Effective Date:** April 1, 2024
**Applies to:** All employees, contractors, and interns

## 1. Asset Allocation
*   **Standard Allocation:** Every full-time employee will be issued a standard company laptop (Windows or Mac, depending on the department) and a headset.
*   **Developers/Designers:** May request high-performance workstations and up to two external monitors via the IT Service Desk.

## 2. Acceptable Use
*   Company assets are provided for business purposes. Occasional, reasonable personal use is permitted provided it does not violate security policies.
*   Installation of unauthorized, pirated, or non-business software is strictly prohibited.
*   All data stored on company devices is the property of the company and is subject to monitoring.

## 3. Loss or Damage
*   Employees must immediately report lost or stolen assets to the IT Helpdesk and Local Security within **24 hours**.
*   In case of theft, a formal police report must be filed and submitted to HR.
*   The company bears the cost of the first accidental damage repair. Repeated negligence may result in the employee covering repair costs.

## 4. Return of Assets
*   Upon termination of employment or contract, all physical IT assets must be returned to the IT department on or before the final working day. Failure to do so may result in legal action or withholding of final settlement funds.